## SQ-RB-21 | Copper Pot recycles a bowl-food ingredient's bowl into the container (1 meal)
@group A
@commands `/setblock` a lit campfire and `miners_delight:copper_pot` on it; `/data merge block` the pot's slots 0-3 with a bowl-served FD cooking recipe that takes a bowl-food ingredient (probe the recipe manager for a `farmersdelight:cooking` recipe whose ingredient has a bowl remainder and whose container is a bowl), container slot (5) empty; wait for one cook; `/data get block`. Repeat with 3 meals' inputs and 1 bowl in slot 5
@pass First case: slot 6 holds the plated meal, slots 5 and 7 empty, no item entity near the pot. Second (rule of 2026-11-03, remainder_buffer.md 3.8): recycled bowls stack in slot 5 up to 64, slot 7 holds only non-bowl leftovers; every bowl accounted for (bowls before = slot 5 + slot 7 + meals plated)
@fails `CopperPotBlockEntity.recycleRoom` / `storeOrThrowLeftover`; `getContainer()` empty because `mealContainerStack` was not set before the leftovers
@from batches/r1102b/s5_R_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# self-contained since r1120fix (2026-11-20): own s5home marker and S5H capture (was the r1102b boot's S5H, never captured when the row runs alone)
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s5home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home,limit=1] Pos
capture S5H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {S5H1+44} {S5H3+12} {S5H1+60} {S5H3+28}
sleep 3
> s5 potrecipe
waitlog \[s5\] potrecipe: \d+ found 30
capture S5PA \[s5\] potnbt1 \S+ (\{.*\})$
capture S5PB \[s5\] potnbt3 \S+ (\{.*\})$
capture S5PC \[s5\] potrecipe \S+ cook (\d+)
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock {S5H1+50} {S5H2} {S5H3+20} minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+20} miners_delight:copper_pot
> data merge block {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+20} {S5PA}
> cdevtest tickwarp {S5PC+300}
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks={S5PC+300} 120
> data get block {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+20}
> cdevtest items {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+20} 2
expect has the following block data: .*\{(?=[^{}]*Slot: 6b?\b)[^{}]*\}.*miners_delight:copper_pot
reject has the following block data: .*\{[^{}]*Slot: [57]b?\b[^{}]*\}.*miners_delight:copper_pot
expect verb=items items=- stacks=0\b
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ .*error=
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|does not (have|accept)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|That position is not loaded|No player was found|no such bot|no such item|Invalid (block state|tag)|\[(zq|s5)\] (error|no player))
look the probe's recipe (potrecipe line) takes a bowl food; slot 6 holds the plated meal; no recipe found = row N/A, not a FAIL
look tick warp {S5PC}+300 ticks replaces the old real-time wait (cook time + 15 s)

## SQ-RB-22 | Pickling Jar recycles a container ingredient's leftover into the container slot
@group A
@commands Place `vintagedelight:fermenting_jar`; probe for a fermenting recipe with a container ingredient whose input leaves that container; `/data merge block` ingredients for 3 batches and 1 container in slot 6; wait 3 x processing time; `/data get block`
@pass 3 outputs in slot 7; slot 6 holds 1 container; slot 9 empty or holding only the extra leftovers; no item entity on the jar. No such recipe in the pack: note it, the row is N/A
@fails `FermentingJarBlockEntity.recycleRoom` (container taken before the leftovers); `remaindersFit` stalls when slot 9 is full
@from batches/r1102b/s5_R_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
